{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other","id":1341526,"title":"How are Psi, Quantum and Flux related to each other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-15T17:29:39-07:00","id":1341526,"title":"How are Psi, Quantum and Flux related to each other?","content":"I\u2019m not sure if there is an official answer yet, but I\u2019m curious about what you guys are doing in your campaigns. Our group probably won\u2019t start playing TC till Aberrant comes out, but it helps to figure out stuff like this in advance so I can get a better feel for my character and the world around her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T23:57:26-07:00","id":1341581,"title":"","content":"It what way do you mean? I\u2019m not sure precisely what aspects your asking after from your post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T03:46:05-07:00","id":1341610,"title":"","content":"Are they three aspects of the same force, or are they three separate forces? Are Psi, Quantum and Flux three different kinds of telluric energy, or is telluric energy just a word they used in Adventure! because people didn\u2019t understand how the universe worked back then?<br /> <br /> Hope this helps clarify what I meant. You\u2019re a writer for Trinity, so you would know the \u201cofficial answer\u201d if anyone would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T05:22:18-07:00","id":1341617,"title":"","content":"Flux and psi are defined in TC Core.Flux is the energies created when two continuum worlds collide with one another. It\u2019s a strain on the fabric of the universe that may create strangeness and that some people may be able to harness. Psi is the inherent psionic power that permeates the universe. Quantum is the fundamental universal forces that govern energy and matter. They\u2019re all three separate \u2018energies\u2019 and not aspects of the same thing.<br /> <br /> The answer to your second question is a little circular. \u2018Telluric energy\u2019 was a term used to describe the poorly understood energy and abilities drawn upon by Daredevils, Stalwarts and Mesmerists in the 1e Adventure! era. The people of that time didn\u2019t understand the differences between the forces, and in 1e the opposing aspects of psi and quantum didn\u2019t manifest as problems for Mesmerists or stalwarts going against each other, for whatever unexplored reason.<br /> <br /> So, by definition, psi, quantum and flux are three different kinds of \u2018telluric energy\u2019 simply because the term \u2018telluric energy\u2019 was invented to describe something the people of the time didn\u2019t really understand. It doesn\u2019t actually mean anything, or that \u2018telluric energy\u2019 is a thing that exists on its own.<br /> <br /> But, caveat this with the fact that 2e Adventure! hasn\u2019t been written yet. Until it is, and it\u2019s published, it\u2019s not established what from 1e carries through to 2e and what doesn\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T10:51:48-07:00","id":1341649,"title":"","content":"The fact that the same genetic sequence can be flipped to three different things is interesting. It makes me curious as to why that genetic structure leads to them all. Now, I assume that a meta-reason is that we don't want a person to be like &quot;I am a Talented Psiad Nova&quot; and such but to me the internal reason is also very interesting to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T17:27:35-07:00","id":1341744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341649#post1341649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the same genetic sequence can be flipped to three different things is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, two different things. Psychomorph or eximorph. Genes don't factor into whatever happens to Talents.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T17:33:07-07:00","id":1341745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341744#post1341744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, two different things. Psychomorph or eximorph. Genes don't factor into whatever happens to Talents.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does that mean someone who has the gene cannot manifest as a Talent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T18:04:48-07:00","id":1341747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341744#post1341744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, two different things. Psychomorph or eximorph. Genes don't factor into whatever happens to Talents.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh really, how interesting. I thought it was all three. Cool stuff though. It totally works with the whole 'Talents are something else' thing. How interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T18:14:39-07:00","id":1341751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341747#post1341747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooooh really, how interesting. I thought it was all three. Cool stuff though. It totally works with the whole 'Talents are something else' thing. How interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. There's an example Talent in the core book who got her powers because she sat in her favorite stairwell to watch the stars for a few hours when there happened to be a flux event going on, and then noticed she had incredible luck later on and decided to use it for crime.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about the whole setup, other than the way it reinforces the &quot;there's lots of alternate realities out there&quot; as something to build campaigns and adventures and characters around, is that it also implies that there could be more power sources. Especially with the (I think new to 2e?) thing where the Hammersmith Experiment was not the first time any of these powers existed, just the first time there was a massive scale event. So there could also be chi or elemental magic or whatever, and ancient X-Men Apocalypse-style nova warlords, rather than everything being strictly bound within the &quot;three games, three sets of powers, everything fits neatly into this scheme, no novas before Divis Mal&quot; thing from 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T18:54:33-07:00","id":1341754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341751#post1341751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. There's an example Talent in the core book who got her powers because she sat in her favorite stairwell to watch the stars for a few hours when there happened to be a flux event going on, and then noticed she had incredible luck later on and decided to use it for crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Novas erupt in kind of the same way, just with Quantum Flux instead of Flux, that\u2019s why in the Nova era there were so many novas. But they had the genetic predisposition to erupt, like Hulk, if instead of Banner, another person was there the person would die, but banned had a genetic capacity of absorbing gamma (or what ever, can\u2019t remember the exact plot).<br /> <br /> Talents may be different, but maybe they have some kind of genetic disposition, or other kind of disposition, like you unknowingly traveled to another reality or maybe you lack a counterpart in a specific parallel reality... just guessing, Flux is the inter dimensional energy, so... any kind of thing is possible.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T19:00:16-07:00","id":1341756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341744#post1341744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, two different things. Psychomorph or eximorph. Genes don't factor into whatever happens to Talents.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is a thing on talents, they can be false positive on Nova gene, as we can see on Nakamura process being used in some people that became Talents and not a Superior, and it\u2019s fairly common with about a Talent for every 5 superiors. As I said, it\u2019s a false positive, possibly a coincidence or a different gene that react in a specific way and have nothing to do with Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T19:20:04-07:00","id":1341759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341751#post1341751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially with the (I think new to 2e?) thing where the Hammersmith Experiment was not the first time any of these powers existed, just the first time there was a massive scale event. So there could also be chi or elemental magic or whatever, and ancient X-Men Apocalypse-style nova warlords, rather than everything being strictly bound within the &quot;three games, three sets of powers, everything fits neatly into this scheme, no novas before Divis Mal&quot; thing from 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not new to 2e its just that the Trinity Broad Gameline ended with Adventure! the Core book so there was no way to really explore other places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T19:20:18-07:00","id":1341760,"title":"","content":"One of the things I like about Trinity is that its all scientific rather than magical or supernatural. That there is an underlying science to Quantum, Psi, or the Flux that Talents use. That given time a species can genetically engineer Quantum, Psi, and such to create variants from the norm. We see it with the Doyn on Psions and we see it with humanity on Superiors. Nothing says that given time other variations couldn't be created by one group or another attempting to create the 'perfect superhuman'. <br /> <br /> Its a nifty concept. Very fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T21:12:42-07:00","id":1341776,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> thank you. That really clarifies things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T22:22:12-07:00","id":1341789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341760#post1341760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I like about Trinity is that its all scientific rather than magical or supernatural. That there is an underlying science to Quantum, Psi, or the Flux that Talents use. That given time a species can genetically engineer Quantum, Psi, and such to create variants from the norm. We see it with the Doyn on Psions and we see it with humanity on Superiors. Nothing says that given time other variations couldn't be created by one group or another attempting to create the 'perfect superhuman'.<br /> <br /> Its a nifty concept. Very fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It really is in how one looks at it. From the scientifically rational outlook in the 21st century, there are natural forces at work that help to produce Novas, Psiads/Psions and Talents, but even during this time, these forces are not fully understood by those researching them. However, if you were to look at them through the superstitous eyes common before the Enlightenment of the 16th Century, one would easily come to the conclusion that these abilities were supernatural in some way. Even Dev Mal referred to the three groups as likely giving rise to the legends of Heroes, Mystics and Gods of antiquity (at least in 1st Ed).<br /> <br /> As the old quote says, sufficiently advanced science/technology would be virtually impossible to distinguish from magic/sorcery by those who didn't understand the difference. What seems like a marvel of science today would be seen as a miracle in another age and time.<br /> <br /> This was my way of thinking when I proposed an alternative setting that would see the powers of Talents, Psions/Psiads and Novas appear in a much earlier era... a Mythic Age that would be remembered in legends of giving rise to mythical nations... of which Atlantis was but one of them. It was going to span 1000 years of time, from the advent of the appearance of these sources of power, through the rise of many mythic nations as these powers mature, to an ultimate crisis that sees most of what was wrought in this age be torn apart as these nations war with each other for dominance... which ultimately sees these sources of power virtually vanish until near the Modern Age (with small pockets of expression popping up from time to time, but not in the same numbers as during this mythic age).<br /> <br /> As I said... it really depends on one's perspective on whether it is science or the supernatural. Today we see lightning as a natural expression of electro-magnetism... but to the Vikings who worshiped Thor... it was his divine wrath made manifest. We understand the principles that cause volcanoes to erupt... but to the Romans living on Pompeii centuries ago, the eruption of Mt. Vesuvius was nothing less than the wrath of Vulcan unleashed upon the world for some unknown offense. By the same token, there may be some things we would see as magical that are merely more advanced principles of science that we do not understand ourselves. The Biotech of Aeon seems almost magical in how it can self repair and even be tailored to the use of a specific individual... relying upon principles of genetics and noetics that we in the 21st century can barely grasp. Magic and Science can often be seen as two different explanations for the same phenomena (depending on one's understanding of the principles involved).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T22:25:57-07:00","id":1341790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341760#post1341760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I like about Trinity is that its all scientific rather than magical or supernatural. That there is an underlying science to Quantum, Psi, or the Flux that Talents use. That given time a species can genetically engineer Quantum, Psi, and such to create variants from the norm. We see it with the Doyn on Psions and we see it with humanity on Superiors. Nothing says that given time other variations couldn't be created by one group or another attempting to create the 'perfect superhuman'. <br /> <br /> Its a nifty concept. Very fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, there's the Heterodyne corollary to Clark's Third Law: a sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from Science. I think we're going to be seeing a bit of that with the Aegis setting and its gods, sorcerers, and heroes, when they get around to it. <br /> <br /> I'd also say that the three types that we've been given have a tremendous flexibility, such that it will be hard to find something that's difficult to fit into one of them. Especially since it's possible for them to manifest differently in different eras. Magic probably fits best with the Noetic spectrum with seers being clairvoyants and elementalists being psychokinetics (though blessings and curses are probably more of an uber-Talent thing); and Chi is traditionally described in the context of skill use, making it also a potential uber-Talent thing (see Exalted, specifically the Solar Exalted, for some ideas of what uber-Talents might be able to do). <br /> <br /> I'm thinking that in the proposed TC:Aegis setting, the gods should be rare compared to heroes and sorcerers, but should manifest closer to Nova-level power so that they can have power over the elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:08:25-07:00","id":1341819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341756#post1341756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a thing on talents, they can be false positive on Nova gene, as we can see on Nakamura process being used in some people that became Talents and not a Superior, and it\u2019s fairly common with about a Talent for every 5 superiors. As I said, it\u2019s a false positive, possibly a coincidence or a different gene that react in a specific way and have nothing to do with Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can also be turned into baselines by the Kaga-2 retrovirus apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T22:01:56-07:00","id":1342016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341745#post1341745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Does that mean someone who has the gene cannot manifest as a Talent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> People with the nova/psion gene do not generally become Talents, no. Or vice versa.<br /> <br /> It's like in the WoD, the Messengers never contact ghouls or kinfolk or sorcerers for the Imbuing. Nothing's stopping them from doing so, they just don't do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1341751#post1341751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially with the (I think new to 2e?) thing where the Hammersmith Experiment was not the first time any of these powers existed, just the first time there was a massive scale event.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was implied in 1e, and it was Bates' intent, but it was never really explicit. Adventure! 1e has Doctor Primoris speculating that in the ancient world, daredevils were heroes, mesmerists were sorcerers, and stalwarts were gods. The Aberrant Players Guide had a sensationalist headline: JESUS WAS A NOVA!!! Aberrant: Project Utopia noted a 1964 event where an unknown person seems to have pushed two cars out of the path of an oncoming train. It's after 1922, but it's well outside any of the pre-defined eras.<br /> <br /> We're just taking that ball and rolling with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T02:29:07-07:00","id":1342042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1342016#post1342016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was implied in 1e, and it was Bates' intent, but it was never really explicit. Adventure! 1e has Doctor Primoris speculating that in the ancient world, daredevils were heroes, mesmerists were sorcerers, and stalwarts were gods. The Aberrant Players Guide had a sensationalist headline: JESUS WAS A NOVA!!! Aberrant: Project Utopia noted a 1964 event where an unknown person seems to have pushed two cars out of the path of an oncoming train. It's after 1922, but it's well outside any of the pre-defined eras.<br /> <br /> We're just taking that ball and rolling with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I liked to look at it in 1e was that the energies from the Hammersmith explosion rippled backwards and forwards through time. Therefore there were no talents, psions or novas before the Hammersmith event, but from the moment it exploded they always existed across all time. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s one of those multiple worlds/continuum thingies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:28:39-07:00","id":1342101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1341526-how-are-psi-quantum-and-flux-related-to-each-other?p=1342042#post1342042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I liked to look at it in 1e was that the energies from the Hammersmith explosion rippled backwards and forwards through time. Therefore there were no talents, psions or novas before the Hammersmith event, but from the moment it exploded they always existed across all time.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s one of those multiple worlds/continuum thingies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that the Hammersmith Event resonated back and forth through time is an intriguing and interesting and fun one. It leads to all sorts of ideas and potentials. <br /> <br /> Imagine it going back or forth and interacting with something being done. Example. It resonates forward to when the first nuclear bomb is detonated and the famous worlds about man becoming like death, destroyer of worlds, imagine the energies hooking on that and doing something, twisting something. <br /> <br /> Or imagine it moving forward in time to when we first activated a particle accelerator, it hooked on to it, causing change. <br /> <br /> Or,maybe, it connected with a meterorite that crashed onto Earth thousands of years ago, changing it, and bringing forth an age of gods. <br /> <br /> You know, just sayin. hehe<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I LOVE, LOVE, LOVE the fact that this edition of Trinity is a Continuum rather than a single world timeline. It makes for all sorts of possibilities. <br /> <br /> I really hope that Onyx Path finds the TC universe financially and socially beneficial so that in time we can have as many, or even more, settings and books in it as we do in World/Chronicles of Darkness. We need the light to push back the darkness. (hehe, campy I know, but I couldn't resist, lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}